      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For MyCorp, the process begins by entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening sentence establishes the process context and trigger (init), explicitly names starting the process (n1), and defines the initial action (n2)."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After entering expenses, the next step is to generate a spreadsheet."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly specifies the spreadsheet generation step following expense entry."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the spreadsheet is generated, the request can be approved or disapproved."
      ],
      "justification": "Describes the first approval decision point, supporting both the action node and the XOR branch gateway."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the request is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Maps to the feedback loop action returning to expense entry upon rejection."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the request is approved, the expenses can be paid out."
      ],
      "justification": "Corresponds to the payment action on the positive branch of the first decision."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The process then checks again if the request is approved or not."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly describes the second sequential approval check, matching the action and branch elements."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Second instance of the rejection feedback loop to expense entry."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "But if it is approved, the expenses can be paid out."
      ],
      "justification": "Second instance of the payout action on the positive branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, after the expenses are paid out, the process comes to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly signals the completion of the process and final termination step."
    }
